message: "If you use or reference this specification, please cite it as below."
title: "Zero-trust AI operations: definition and five rules"
abstract: >-
  Zero-trust AI operations is zero trust applied to the AI that runs your IT
  operations. The AI gets real reach: it reads each system through its
  vendor's own API and drafts the fix. It gets no standing trust: its code has
  no network, it holds no credentials, it cannot approve, and every change
  waits for a person and is recorded. Five rules map the definition to the
  tenets of NIST SP 800-207, with a 25-question checklist.
